WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.992 --> 00:00:04.470
- [Narrator] This video was
filmed at a hospital in Wuhan,

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:07.130
the center of the coronavirus epidemic.

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:11.047
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:21.066 --> 00:00:23.918
And this is footage of a
hospital under construction.

00:00:23.918 --> 00:00:28.163
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:28.163 --> 00:00:30.043
Behind the camera are two vloggers,

00:00:30.043 --> 00:00:32.343
who have become sensations in China.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.930
Fang Bin is a resident of Wuhan

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:38.430
and Chen Qiushi, a human rights lawyer.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:40.470
The two vloggers who were known in China

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:44.270
as citizen journalists published
unfiltered video reports

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:48.060
as the crisis unfolded in late
January and early February,

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.350
scenes that haven't appeared

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:52.330
in China's tightly controlled state media.

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:56.247
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:58.293 --> 00:01:01.523
But they stopped posting
videos in early February.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.540
(scuffling)

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:08.221
Fellow activists and relatives
said they have disappeared.

00:01:08.221 --> 00:01:11.020
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:12.650
Chen's mother posted a video

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:15.487
saying she wasn't able to contact her son,

00:01:15.487 --> 00:01:18.500
according to a friend, the
police told Chen's father,

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:20.793
that his son was held in quarantine.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.350
Activists say neighbors of Fang

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:26.070
saw a uniformed and plain
clothes police officers

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:29.423
take him away, the activists
haven't seen him since.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:33.210
Even if their images were
only available online

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:37.370
for days or even hours, China
experts say it is unusual

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:40.430
for Beijing authorities to let
this form of open criticism

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:43.040
appear before censoring content

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:45.550
or clamping down on its creators.

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:48.942
Many citizens have spoken
up from doctors and nurses

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:51.499
to people stuck at home and patients,

00:01:51.499 --> 00:01:55.416
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:58.480
challenging the official narrative

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:01.520
of hospitals being
speedily built from scratch

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:02.705
and armies of volunteers

00:02:02.705 --> 00:02:06.010
orderly working to contain the epidemic.

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:08.128
So how are these videos
critical of authorities

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:10.163
getting out into the public?

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:13.698
Beijing officials have said
there is a genuine desire

00:02:13.698 --> 00:02:16.811
to promote accurate
information about the epidemic

00:02:16.811 --> 00:02:20.440
and block false reports
that could increase panic.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:23.170
Nonetheless the anger in
China came to a tipping point

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:25.958
late January after people
accused local authorities

00:02:25.958 --> 00:02:28.244
of trying to cover up what was happening.

00:02:28.244 --> 00:02:33.020
- [Bao] People was not informed
in the three to four weeks.

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:37.704
What we have witnessed is the
revolt of the Chinese people.

00:02:37.704 --> 00:02:40.710
- [Narrator] Bao Pu publishes
books from Hong Kong

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:43.520
on topics that are censored by Beijing.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:45.181
He says people grew
frustrated when they saw

00:02:45.181 --> 00:02:48.697
the healthcare system was
overwhelmed by the coronavirus,

00:02:48.697 --> 00:02:50.860
especially after the SARS epidemic,

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:54.584
that took nearly 800
lives in 2002 and 2003.

00:02:54.584 --> 00:02:57.043
- [Bao] People generally
expect the government

00:02:57.043 --> 00:03:01.100
have learned the lessons
of the SARS epidemic,

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.604
so they should have
developed various mechanisms

00:03:03.604 --> 00:03:06.021
to prevent that from ever happening.

00:03:06.021 --> 00:03:07.950
- [Narrator] Pu says the speed

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.831
at which the criticism piled
up online might be too hard

00:03:10.831 --> 00:03:13.409
for China's censorship apparatus to manage

00:03:13.409 --> 00:03:15.070
and that is one reason Chinese citizens

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:17.790
have managed to share content online.

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:19.292
Tens of millions have been stuck at home

00:03:19.292 --> 00:03:21.284
leading to a surge in the number of people

00:03:21.284 --> 00:03:24.040
reading and using social media.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:26.410
Another explanation
according to researchers

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:28.080
might be that in this situation,

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.555
Beijing needs information to keep flowing.

00:03:30.555 --> 00:03:32.042
- Because this is a health crisis,

00:03:32.042 --> 00:03:35.186
people also need to talk
about supplies and access

00:03:35.186 --> 00:03:36.815
and they need to be able to discuss this,

00:03:36.815 --> 00:03:38.978
otherwise they're kind of stuck
at home in quarantine zones

00:03:38.978 --> 00:03:40.687
and it becomes really insufferable,

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:42.736
so they can't completely
censor all discussions.

00:03:42.736 --> 00:03:45.070
- [Narrator] Maria Repnikova analyzes

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:47.025
how Beijing censors its citizens

00:03:47.025 --> 00:03:48.880
and says she believes the government

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:50.896
intentionally opened
the doors to criticism.

00:03:50.896 --> 00:03:52.692
- It's useful in some ways to
learn about what's happening,

00:03:52.692 --> 00:03:54.779
while it's only the early
stages of the crisis,

00:03:54.779 --> 00:03:57.320
the state officials at
the local central level

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:59.412
still don't quite know
what are the bigger issues,

00:03:59.412 --> 00:04:00.639
what are the big frustrations,

00:04:00.639 --> 00:04:04.336
it's kind of a way to get
public opinion on this,

00:04:04.336 --> 00:04:07.109
try to understand the grievances
and then respond to that.

00:04:07.109 --> 00:04:08.580
- [Narrator] Repnikova has interviewed

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:12.361
over 100 Chinese journalists
and officials about big crises

00:04:12.361 --> 00:04:16.303
like mining disasters or
the 2008 Sichuan earthquake.

00:04:17.228 --> 00:04:20.450
She noticed there's a
limited window of opportunity

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:22.380
for journalists to cover these events

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:24.510
and citizens to complain.

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:27.045
Repnikova says during
the Sichuan earthquake,

00:04:27.045 --> 00:04:29.285
the government started
to tape mouths shut,

00:04:29.285 --> 00:04:31.726
when journalists reported
that poorly built schools

00:04:31.726 --> 00:04:35.490
had contributed to the deaths
of hundreds of children.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:38.120
In Wuhan, Fang Bin was able to publish

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:41.880
33 videos in 16 days on YouTube.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.720
One video he posted online
shows that he had run ins

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.074
with people who identified themselves

00:04:46.074 --> 00:04:47.729
as local health officials,

00:04:47.729 --> 00:04:49.403
who wanted to check Fang's health,

00:04:49.403 --> 00:04:51.723
because he had visited a hospital.

00:04:51.723 --> 00:04:55.640
(speaking in foreign language)

00:04:58.549 --> 00:05:00.882
(scuffling)

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:08.570
Fang said the men confiscated
his computer and phone,

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:10.820
then drove him to the
outskirts of the city

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:12.403
to continue questioning him,

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:16.753
activists say he disappeared a week later.

00:05:16.753 --> 00:05:19.583
(sobbing)

00:05:19.583 --> 00:05:21.870
A Chinese diplomat was asked about Fang

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:22.703
during a TV interview.

00:05:22.703 --> 00:05:25.810
- So I believe the relevant authorities

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:28.631
and departments in China,
the legal departments

00:05:28.631 --> 00:05:31.627
are dealing with the case
in accordance with law.

00:05:31.627 --> 00:05:35.544
(speaking in foreign language)

00:05:38.897 --> 00:05:41.530
- [Narrator] Authorities
have made no public statement

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:44.683
about Chen's disappearance
or Fang's whereabouts.

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:48.219
The disappearance of both
men in early February

00:05:48.219 --> 00:05:50.990
happened around the time
when the death toll in China

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:54.110
came closer to surpassing
the one from SARS.

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:55.796
This is also approximately when Beijing

00:05:55.796 --> 00:05:58.728
began ramping up efforts
to create a new narrative

00:05:58.728 --> 00:06:01.460
that things were under control.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:03.968
Even though Chinese officials
have continually offered

00:06:03.968 --> 00:06:07.354
assurances that the epidemic
is being successful managed,

00:06:07.354 --> 00:06:11.271
(speaking in foreign language)

00:06:12.548 --> 00:06:15.180
state controlled media
have now put the blame

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:17.169
on local authorities for a slow response

00:06:17.169 --> 00:06:19.061
to contain the outbreak in Wuhan,

00:06:19.061 --> 00:06:20.907
while praising central authorities

00:06:20.907 --> 00:06:24.713
for quickly pouring resources
into the center of the crisis.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:27.652
- Many of these crises
are also opportunities

00:06:27.652 --> 00:06:31.130
for political systems to come
out as the winners or victors

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:33.569
or kind of as being in charge
of this state of affairs.

00:06:33.569 --> 00:06:34.727
- [Narrator] About a month

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:37.014
after the disappearance of Chen and Fang,

00:06:37.014 --> 00:06:39.700
health officials said the
number of new infections

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:41.444
had fallen dramatically in China,

00:06:41.444 --> 00:06:44.590
authorities reported new
infections in double digits,

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:47.451
down from hundreds of cases a day.

00:06:47.451 --> 00:06:51.280
The outcry on Chinese social
media, even if short lived

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:53.940
shows that many people
in the country don't buy

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:57.033
the government's message that
the crisis is under control.

00:06:57.923 --> 00:07:00.254
(somber string music)

